CORE (was KNOWNBUG; header-free, cvise-reduced-then-repaired isolation of
cpp17_tuple_basic).  Mirrors libstdc++ std::tuple: a variadic converting
constructor guarded by a defaulted SFINAE template parameter whose condition is a
two-parallel-pack fold over the class pack and the constructor's own pack
(`_TupleConstraints<_Elements...>::ic<_UElements...>()` ==
`and_<is_ctible<_Elements,_UElements>::value...>::value`), plus `get<I>` via
derived-to-base deduction of the `_Tuple_impl<I,...>` base.  This is greened by
the recursive non-type / bool parameter-pack fixes (the recursive `and_<...>`
fold over a partial specialization with an empty deduced trailing pack now
evaluates); make_tuple constructs the tuple and get<0> reads the constructed
value.  Both g++ and clang++ run it with get<0> == 1.
